From afb25a31f37ab687ebd1645e386f9e82ffd043b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Release Radar <release-radar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:28:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Start from the phone; the server's position wins only
 when another device set it

The last book starts without the server: the home page shows the shelves
the server sent last time while the connection is still being made (covers
from the saved config, a tap starts the book), Android Auto answers at once
with the cached Continue list, and tapping the last book reuses its session
and the cached audio. Before the server has answered, the saved config
stands in for the session it created.

Every streamed book plays from the library files with the current token, so
a session the server dropped, or a refreshed token, cannot break a stream;
a dropped session is renewed on the first failed sync without touching the
player.

After a cached start, or play after a longer pause, the server is asked
where the book is, and asked again until it answers; until then this phone
holds its own progress syncs and does not save them for the web layer to
upload. The server wins only when it holds a position this phone never got
it to accept; a finished record never wins; a seek by the listener turns a
jump into an offer. Both positions stay one tap away: a single tappable
notice, the player menu, and a button on the car screen.

Positions are recorded per book and episode; a finished book starts over;
a position the reconcile only parked at is never recorded as this phone's.
The pre-buffer learns the audio offset on any network and downloads windows
on Wi-Fi only; the audio length comes from the mdat box. Home route: a
network change re-proves the address at once, a probe that started on the
old network is dropped, a failed probe retries with backoff, a token refresh
re-proves it. A crash leaves its stack trace on the Logs page; log masking
covers configured hosts with and without ports.

Seven adversarial review rounds (41, 21, 16, 14, 13, 8 and 8 confirmed
findings) plus a narrow check of the final edit are folded in. Known and
left for the next patch: a sync the server applied without a reply can
look like another device's move; a cast switch during an unanswered
server check; re-tapping the playing book in the car drops the way back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

